  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coalition for Farmer Allied Intermediaries (CFAI) Wimssy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this grant is to improve the living standards of 4,000 dairy farmers in Kiambu County out of which 49% are women. The organisation buys an average of 5,000 litres of milk daily from the 4,000dairy farmers and process them into yoghurt and pasterised milk with three days shelf life. They want to introduce a new product with expanded shelf life of 90 days. This has been neccesitated by Covid 19 pandemic that has saw increased demand for long life milk for stocking due to goverment restrictions on movements through lockdowns and curfews. The grant will also help the grantee to comply with the recent goverment regulations that organisations should ensure they ensure they put all necessary measures to prevent new cases of covid 19 infections.</narrative>
  </description>
